      "message": "[error] Line 112: 🔴 The pointer overload only rejects a ban when `cert-\u003egetLongId()` matches the current account certificate. The account identity and TrustStore permission key are the certificate\u0027s short `getId()` (`accountUri_`), so a reissued/alternate certificate for the same account identity with a different long ID can still be banned through this overload. Reject `BANNED` when `cert-\u003egetId().toString() \u003d\u003d accountUri_` as well, while retaining the long-ID check if needed.",
